BT /F1 12 Tf 72 720 Td 14 TL (Data classification) Tj T* ( ) Tj T* (Data at Larkspur Labs belongs to one of three classes. Public data may be) Tj T* (shared with anyone. Internal data may be shared with colleagues and) Tj T* (contractors under contract. Confidential data, which includes all customer) Tj T* (data and personal data about employees, is shared only with people who need it) Tj T* (for their work.) Tj T* ( ) Tj T* (Confidential data is never pasted into external tools, including translation) Tj T* (sites and chat assistants that are not approved by the security team.) Tj T* ( ) Tj T* (Phishing) Tj T* ( ) Tj T* (Report suspicious emails with the report button in your email client rather) Tj T* (than forwarding them. The security team runs a phishing exercise every) Tj T* (quarter; clicking a test link is not punished, but it is followed by a short) Tj T* (training.) Tj T* ( ) Tj T* (Access reviews) Tj T* ( ) Tj T* (Managers review the access of their team members every quarter and remove) Tj T* (access that is no longer needed. When someone leaves the company, all of their) Tj T* (access is removed on their last working day.) Tj T* ( ) Tj T* (Reporting vulnerabilities) Tj T* ( ) Tj T* (If you find a security weakness in our product, report it to the security team) Tj T* (rather than testing it further. External researchers can report) Tj T* (vulnerabilities through the security page on our website.) Tj T* ET
